# L §2.5 binding order, E §4.1 the movement order (tally 2.1.2, issue #39, the user's "B: by day, then typed order"): an
# ask's binding over movements runs by day, then the movement order compared typed: keys of a list index in index
# order, so rent[f3] before rent[f11] (tally 2.1.1 compared the order's text, and key position 10 sorted before 2).
# zfee, on an earlier day, comes first whatever its id.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index flats = [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8, f9, f10, f11]
input rent_amt: money PLN
input fee_amt: money PLN
input rent_day: date
input fee_day: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move rent[f in flats]: transfers
  on rent_day
  when pos(f) == 3 or pos(f) == 11
  leg cash from konto to world amount rent_amt

move zfee: transfers
  on fee_day
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee_amt

ask q: x.cash.amount for x in transfers over 2026-02

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 10.00 PLN
  fee_amt = 1.00 PLN
  rent_day = 2026-02-03
  fee_day = 2026-02-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q (x = zfee): 1.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: zfee
  cut 2026-06-30
q (x = rent[f3]): 10.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[f3]
  cut 2026-06-30
q (x = rent[f11]): 10.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: rent[f11]
  cut 2026-06-30
